---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { siteName, supportEmail } from '../config/site';
---

<DocLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy - Files Never Leave Your Device | ${siteName}`}
  description={`How ${siteName} handles your files and data. Short answer: it doesn't, everything runs on your device. No uploads, no accounts, no cookies, no analytics.`}
  heading="Privacy"
  updated="Last updated October 2026"
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    {siteName} is a static site with no backend. As of the date above every tool runs inside your browser,
    so there is no server to receive your files. You don't have to take our word for it: the whole thing
    is open source, so you can read exactly what any tool does, or <a href="/privacy-proof"
      >check it live</a
    >.
  </Fragment>

  <section>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing from your files, and no accounts, analytics, tracking scripts, advertising, or
      cookies. The only record is the server logs described under Hosting.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare serves the site and, like any host, records standard access logs: IP address, page
      requested, timestamp, user agent, and similar technical data. We also keep Cloudflare's
      request logs and traces switched on to watch performance and catch errors. We add no analytics
      on top and don't use any of this to identify anyone. Your files are never part of it, because
      they never leave your device. Fonts are self-hosted, and no third-party font, analytics, or
      advertising service is loaded.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal data
      held about you. In practice we hold none unless you've emailed us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>. Emailing us means we receive your
      address and whatever you include, used only to reply and never added to a list.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocLayout>
